establish that $γ(P(m,n))$ is $Θ_n(m^{-2})$ as $m\\to\\infty$. This disproves a conjecture of Blanco and Buehrle asserting that, for fixed $n$, the corresponding undirected generalized pancake graphs form an expander family.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOn the Laplacian spectral gap of generalized pancake graphs - arXiv Combinatorics (https://arxiv.symmetricfunctions.com/paper/2608.15398v1)\nciteturn8search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: last month; ## On the Laplacian spectral gap of generalized pancake graphs ... Published: 2026-08-15 ... The generalized pancake graph $P(m,n)$ is the Cayley graph of the group of colored permutations $\\mathbb{Z}_m\\wr S_n=(\\mathbb{Z}_m)^n\\rtimes S_n$ generated by generalized prefix reversals.\n\n## On the Laplacian spectral gap of generalized pancake graphs\n\nSaúl A. Blanco\n\nPublished: 2026-08-15\n\nComments: 25 pages, 2 figures\n\nNote:\n\nPublication:\n\ncs.DM math.CO\n\ncolored permutation graph group pancake permutation\n\n# • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\n### Abstract\n\nThe generalized pancake graph $P(m,n)$ is the Cayley graph of the group of colored permutations $\\mathbb{Z}_m\\wr S_n=(\\mathbb{Z}_m)^n\\rtimes S_n$ generated by generalized prefix reversals. In this paper, we establish that, for all $m,n\\geq2$, the spectral gap $γ(P(m,n))$ of the normalized Laplacian satisfies $α_m/n\\leqγ(P(m,n))\\leq1/n$, where $α_m$ is a positive constant that depends only on $m$. As a consequence, for every fixed $m\\geq2$, $γ(P(m,n))$ is $Θ_m(1/n)$ as $n\\to\\infty$. The proof combines Cesi's semi-recursive spectral-gap inequality with a Fourier decomposition of the appropriate operators associated with a coset Schreier graph of color-position pairs. For fixed $n\\geq2$, we also establish that $γ(P(m,n))$ is $Θ_n(m^{-2})$ as $m\\to\\infty$. This disproves a conjecture of Blanco and Buehrle asserting that, for fixed $n$, the corresponding undirected generalized pancake graphs form an expander family.\n\n### BibTeX\n\n[Button: arXiv BibTeX ] [Button: Published BibTeX ]\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSpectral-gap equality conjecture for generalised pancake graphs | MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/370305/spectral-gap-equality-conjecture-for-generalised-pancake-gra)\nciteturn8search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; This is proposed from cursory computational evidence and asserts that the spectral gap of the generalised pancake graph is exactly captured by the associated matrix $Q(\\mathfrak P_{m,n})$Q(P m,n​). ... Greaves and Haoran Zhu, “A note on some spectral properties of generalised pancake graphs”, arXiv:2509.09425 (2026).\n\n# Spectral-gap equality conjecture for generalised pancake graphs\n\nAt least 24 years old · documented by 2001\n\nLet $\\mathcal P_m(n)$P m​(n) be the generalised pancake graph and let $Q(\\mathfrak P_{m,n})$Q(P m,n​) be the associated matrix used in the paper. For a symmetric matrix or graph, write $\\lambda_1$λ 1​ and $\\lambda_2$λ 2​ for its largest and second-largest eigenvalues. Spectral-gap equality conjecture. For integers $m\\geqslant 1$m⩾1 and $n\\geqslant 2$n⩾2,\n\n$$\\lambda_1(\\mathcal P_m(n)) - \\lambda_2(\\mathcal P_m(n)) = \\lambda_1(Q(\\mathfrak P_{m,n})) - \\lambda_2(Q(\\mathfrak P_{m,n})).$$λ 1​(P m​(n))−λ 2​(P m​(n))=λ 1​(Q(P m,n​))−λ 2​(Q(P m,n​)).\n\nThis is proposed from cursory computational evidence and asserts that the spectral gap of the generalised pancake graph is exactly captured by the associated matrix $Q(\\mathfrak P_{m,n})$Q(P m,n​). No proof or resolution is supplied in the paper.\n\nReferences\n\n## Primary source\n\nGary R. W. Greaves and Haoran Zhu, “A note on some spectral properties of generalised pancake graphs”, arXiv:2509.09425 (2026).\n\n## Additional references\n\n9 papers in this index state this conjecture (2001–2025). The statement above is taken from the most recent of them; the others are arXiv:25